<title>EGYPT: Egypt seeks 30,000 t yellow corn for Sept/Oct.</title>
<headline>Egypt seeks 30,000 t yellow corn for Sept/Oct.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state's Food Industries Company said on Thursday it wanted to buy 30,000 tonnes of yellow corn for arrival in the second half of September and/or the second half of October.</p>
<p>The corn should be Grade 2 or better and it must be of U.S. or Argentine origin, said Muharram Ghanem, the head of the sales department at the company.</p>
<p>The deadline for bids is noon (0900 GMT) on July 22, he told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 578 3290/1 jw</p>
</text>
